bly playing d4 or maintaining central dominance. Given that White has a bishop on c4 (BWF1), challenging with …c5 fights back effectively. It also prepares …Nc6 or …Qb6 ideas, increasing activity. While N: b8-d7 is safe and good, immediate central counterplay with **c6-c5** offers more dynamic winning chances.\n\nAnswer: P: c6-c5"}
